WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:11,890
So, I ask you this question about the alcohol and phosphatase.

00:00:11,890 --> 00:00:13,890
Still with the normal limits.

00:00:13,890 --> 00:00:21,890
Did they do any other tested to look for any possible metastasis?

00:00:21,890 --> 00:00:27,890
So, if it was me, if I was your oncologist, I may want to just,

00:00:27,890 --> 00:00:33,890
I would possibly suggest a PET scan.

00:00:33,890 --> 00:00:35,890
If they did a PET scan recently,

00:00:35,890 --> 00:00:39,890
when was your last PET scan? That would be my question.

00:00:39,890 --> 00:00:43,890
Again, you're still with the normal limits.

00:00:43,890 --> 00:00:48,890
Certainly, alcohol and phosphatase could rise, so let's talk about that.

00:00:48,890 --> 00:00:51,890
What could cause alcohol and phosphatase to rise?

00:00:51,890 --> 00:00:59,890
Congestion of the liver is the first thing that you think of with elevated alcohol and phosphatase.

00:00:59,890 --> 00:01:05,890
So, someone who does not have a diagnosis of cancer, you think of a congestion of the liver.

00:01:05,890 --> 00:01:13,890
Taking incense, so Tylenol, Advil, can cause elevation of alcohol and phosphatase.

00:01:13,890 --> 00:01:19,890
Taking other medication can cause elevation of alcohol and phosphatase because it's irritant to the liver.

00:01:19,890 --> 00:01:22,890
So, those are your first things that you look at.

00:01:22,890 --> 00:01:28,890
With a diagnosis of cancer, the other thing that can cause elevated alcohol and phosphatase

00:01:28,890 --> 00:01:33,890
is the bony metastasis. So, if there's metastasis to any bone that's causing

00:01:33,890 --> 00:01:38,890
the lytic metastasis will cause elevation in alcohol and phosphatase.

00:01:38,890 --> 00:01:42,890
So, that's a differential diagnosis that you want to rule out.

00:01:42,890 --> 00:01:46,890
What's going on with my liver? Typically, if I have metastasis to my liver from cancer,

00:01:46,890 --> 00:01:49,890
that's not necessarily going to cause elevated alcohol and phosphatase.

00:01:49,890 --> 00:01:55,890
It's congestion of the liver due to a medication usually or some sort of toxin,

00:01:55,890 --> 00:02:01,890
toxic exposure, can cause it as well. That's what you're looking at.

00:02:01,890 --> 00:02:11,890
So, differential diagnosis, elevated alcohol and phosphatase is toxicification to the liver through something,

00:02:11,890 --> 00:02:17,890
or if the person has a diagnosis of cancer, if there's any bony metastasis.

00:02:17,890 --> 00:02:20,890
Those are the things that should be rolled out.

00:02:20,890 --> 00:02:25,890
Again, your alkaline phosphatase is still with a normal limit.

00:02:25,890 --> 00:02:30,890
So, but still, if I was your oncologist, I'd at least suggest, should we do a PET scan?

